````markdown
**Wayfarer: Lares (Tasked Spirit)**

# 1. Ink & Switch — Keyhive, Subduction, Automerge

**The side-branches, decoded.** `subduction` and `authors` are not competing designs — `authors` is a fork *of* subduction.

- The git branch is `subductionjs`, tracked by **PR #601 "Tracking PR: Subduction support" → main, still OPEN and DRAFT** (77 commits, 187 files, updated 2026-08-20). Subduction is **not** converging to main yet; main has none of it. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo/pull/601
- Subduction support lives **inside the `automerge-repo` package itself** (dep `@automerge/automerge-subduction`), plus a new `automerge-repo-storage-lmdb` adapter that main lacks. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo/tree/subductionjs/packages
- **`authors` = subductionjs + "Add automerge signing API"** (commit 2026-06-12), branched 2026-07-03 and **stale since**. Its `@automerge/automerge-subduction` is pinned to 0.16.0 while subductionjs moved to 0.16.1. Treat `authors` as a parked experiment. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo/commits/authors
- **`2.6.0-subduction.48` (2026-08-20) carries a data-loss fix**: "Prevent compaction deleting blobs that could not be decrypted yet" + "Record blob ids into knownHashes on bulk load" (PR #734). If you run .47 or earlier with encryption, you can lose blobs. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo/commits/subductionjs
- Open repro against subductionjs: **`Subduction.getAllHeads` drops fragment heads and advertises boundaries** (#741, 2026-08-27) — unfixed. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo/pull/741

**Subduction is now a public, independent repo** (106 stars, created 2025-07-18, pushed daily).

- Peer-to-peer sync for hash-linked data; Sedimentree for history sharding; explicitly **encryption-friendly — syncs encrypted partitions without decrypting**; transports WebSocket, HTTP long-poll, **Iroh/QUIC**. https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction
- **Sedimentree = depth-based partitioning by leading-zero-byte count of a BLAKE3 digest.** Content-oblivious, deterministic strata. https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction/blob/main/design/sedimentree.md
- **Wire format is a hand-rolled canonical binary codec, explicitly not CBOR** — 4-byte schema header (2-byte prefix `ST`/`SU`, 1-byte type, **1-byte version**), 32-byte Ed25519 issuer VK, fields, 64-byte sig. **Decoders reject unknown prefixes or unsupported versions.** https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction/blob/main/design/protocol.md
- Handshake requires **timestamp freshness, 60s default**, plus nonce tracking and audience binding. A wall-clock dependency that cuts against our clockless lease model. https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction/blob/main/design/security/threats.md
- Recent: **iroh 1.0 upgrade** (#257, 2026-06-23), redb storage backend (#240), per-peer rate limiting (#242), op-set digests for keyhive sync checks (#258), switch to `bijoux` varints (#277). Nightlies only — `v0.16.0-nightly.2026-08-13` is the latest tag. https://github.com/inkandswitch/subduction/commits/main

**Keyhive.** Beelay was **removed from the keyhive workspace** in Oct 2025 (#151); the crate tree is now `beekem` / `keyhive_core` / `keyhive_crypto` / `keyhive_wasm`. Subduction is Beelay's successor. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive

- **#213 (2026-08-15) — BeeKEM replaced path ratcheting with independently sampled secrets.** The stated reason: with ratcheting, *compromising one inner node's secret gave you ancestors you had not compromised.* +11/−66. This is your flag-day. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/pull/213
- **#216 "Fixes for CGKA access" (2026-08-27) is a SECURITY fix and is NOT in alpha.8** (published 2026-08-18). It: limits transitive authority to **the weakest link on the best path**; stops **Relay access to a group transitively granting membership in a document's CGKA tree**; exposes CGKA members via WASM; adds tests that *fail on main before the fix*. +1055/−73. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/pull/216
- #208 (2026-06-26) added application-secret chains, `SymmetricKey::try_seal/try_open`, `force_pcs_update` returning the new leaf secret for sharing across tabs/shared-worker, and public-member CGKA fallbacks. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/pull/208
- Lab note **06 · "E2EE in the Local-First Setting" (2026-07-31)**, guest post by Derek Yen: formalizes BeeKEM security. **No attacks found.** Proves forward secrecy, post-compromise security, and a novel **cross-fork security** property with no analogue in centralized CGKA models. Introduces κ = number of retained individual secrets; κ>1 weakens FS but is needed for partition robustness. https://www.inkandswitch.com/keyhive/notebook/06/

**New projects in the capability/naming space:**

- **`onomancy` — "a local-first name system", created 2026-08-21.** Three name forms over one self-certifying identity: `automerge:3RFyJz…/foo` (doc anchor), `~/bob/pics` (local petname), `@expede.wtf/foo` (DNSSEC-rooted from the baked-in IANA root KSK). Has an `onomancy_keyhive` crate doing **delegation-chain replay behind an `AuthorityVerifier`**. Verified bindings are self-authenticating records, gossipable by QR or Bluetooth. https://github.com/inkandswitch/onomancy
- **`bijou`/`bijoux`** — bijective canonical varints, one encoding per value, big-endian so lexicographic order matches numeric. **Width variants are explicitly NOT wire-compatible.** npm `@inkandswitch/bijoux@0.1.0`. https://github.com/inkandswitch/bijou
- **`bedrock`** — NixOS/DigitalOcean declarative config for a Subduction sync server with Caddy/Prometheus/Grafana/Loki/Tailscale. A ready-made hearth recipe. https://github.com/inkandswitch/bedrock
- **`keyhive-react`** (pre-alpha, `@automerge/keyhive-react@0.1.0-alpha.3`) — `AccountView`, `AccessEditor`, `DirectoryProvider`. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive-react
- **`backstitch`** (Automerge version control for Godot), `pushwork` (CRDT directory sync, npm 2.2.3), `darn`, `patchwork-*`.

**The canonical working stack**, from `@automerge/automerge-repo-keyhive@0.5.0-alpha.7` (ARK, 2026-08-24) dependencies — this is the combination I&S actually runs:

```
@keyhive/keyhive              0.1.0-alpha.8
@automerge/automerge-repo     2.6.0-subduction.48
@automerge/automerge-subduction 0.16.1
@noble/hashes                 ^2.2.0
```
https://registry.npmjs.org/@automerge/automerge-repo-keyhive

**ARK carries a stated demolition notice**: "The TypeScript implementation of the keyhive sync protocol will be removed in the near future in favor of a WASM API for the Rust implementation, which is a major refactor" — naming `sync-protocol.ts`, `keyhive-subduction-adapter.ts`, `codec.ts`, `network-adapter.ts`, `cbor-builder.ts`, `batch.ts`, `pending.ts` as doomed. Do not build against those. https://github.com/automerge/automerge-repo-keyhive

**Automerge core:** 3.4.1 (2026-08-12), 3.4.0 (2026-07-31), 3.3.0 (2026-07-12). Release bodies are empty; the record is in commits.

- **A corruption bug in bool columns was fixed in 3.4.0** (#1482, merged 2026-07-30), fuzz tests upgraded. Data-integrity relevant. https://github.com/automerge/automerge/pull/1482
- **`hexane`** — new columnar encoding engine (1.0.0-alpha.5), a long tail of loader-hardening commits rejecting wrapped lengths and overflowing divisions. `flate2` → `zlib-rs`. `next` tag = `3.4.0-rev-frag-hex.3`.
- **Fragments** (#1446, merged 2026-07-12) — Automerge now tracks history fragments incrementally on load, <1% load cost. This is the core-side support Sedimentree stratification needs. https://github.com/automerge/automerge/issues/1326

Patchwork notebook has six 2026 entries, newest **"Progressions" 2026-05-12**. https://www.inkandswitch.com/patchwork/notebook/

