# 2. Adjacent CRDT sync/auth projects

- **Loro `loro-crdt@1.15.1` (2026-08-29)** — 1.15.0 fixed a **content-redaction leak**: shallow-snapshot export shipped rich-text mark values verbatim for ranges that were fully deleted, defeating the documented redaction use. Exactly our tamper-probe law — assert the *encoding* changed, not the decode. https://github.com/loro-dev/loro/blob/main/crates/loro-wasm/CHANGELOG.md
- **Loro 1.14.1** made `importBatch` atomic with OpLog rollback — a malformed remote blob used to panic *after* leaving the doc detached. Any decoder we expose to peers needs this shape. Same URL.
- **Yjs** — stable `v13.6.32` (2026-08-04, one UndoManager fix); **v14.0.0 still in RC** (`rc.24`, 2026-07-15) with an API rename landed. https://github.com/yjs/yjs/releases
- **y-crdt `v0.27.4` (2026-08-22)** — **"Harden decoders against length-prefix allocation bombs"** plus a `find_index` out-of-range panic fix. https://github.com/y-crdt/y-crdt/compare/v0.27.2...v0.27.4
- **Jazz — ground-up 2.0 rewrite in alpha** (`2.0.0-alpha.53`, 2026-07-10; stable line `0.20.19`). Pivots to a local-first *relational database* with a Rust core. Adds `definePermissions()` with an "Enforcing mode" gated on a **permissions head + bundle pair** — and fixed a race where the head arriving first flipped the client to Enforcing **without an authorization schema**, failing every local write `policy denied`. Any two-part capability admission has that shape. https://github.com/garden-co/jazz/blob/main/packages/jazz-tools/CHANGELOG.md
- **Jazz also added a protocol-version check *in the WebSocket handshake*** (incompatible peers get an explicit update prompt, not a mystery desync) and closed an **unauthenticated LZ4 decompression bomb on the pre-auth handshake**. Same URL. *No source found either way on whether 2.0 retains E2EE — its permissions read as server-enforced row policy.*
- **Evolu `@evolu/web@3.1.1` (2026-09-01)** — Evolu Protocol moved to its own MessagePack-derived codec with three round-trip fixes (nesting-limit symmetry, `-0` preservation, own `__proto__` no longer mangled); values now reject NaN/±Infinity. https://github.com/evoluhq/evolu/blob/main/packages/common/CHANGELOG.md
- **ElectricSQL `@electric-sql/client@1.5.27` (2026-09-01)** — **authentication bypass on `/v1/shape` in secure mode**: auth gated on the *raw path*, so a trailing slash, doubled slash, or percent-encoded char skipped the secret check. Now gates on the router-resolved route. This is our carrier-gradient law in someone else's codebase — read the declaration, never the path. https://github.com/electric-sql/electric/blob/main/packages/sync-service/CHANGELOG.md
- **Iroh `v1.1.0` (2026-08-25); `v1.0.0` shipped 2026-06-15.** 1.1.0 **stopped sending SNI** (#4473) and switched to **random mapped addresses instead of a counter** (#4469) — both cut passive linkability. 1.0.0 added **relay Bearer-token access control with no external service** (#4326). Subduction already rides Iroh 1.0. https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh/releases/tag/v1.1.0
- **DXOS `v0.11.1` (2026-08-05)** — v0.11.0 added **tag-based broadcast pub/sub on a dedicated `onBroadcast` channel**, kept strictly off the point-to-point path (new wire fields `signal.Message.tags`, `SwarmRequest.SUBSCRIBE`). Clean fan-out pattern. https://github.com/dxos/dxos/releases/tag/v0.11.0
- **PowerSync `@powersync/web@2.2.0` (2026-08-13)** — BroadcastChannel shares sync status across tabs when shared workers are off; v2.0.0 moved sync options to `connect()`-time only. https://github.com/powersync-ja/powersync-js/releases
- **Muse is now Allume** — renamed June 2026 over a trademark opportunity, no migration. v4.0 (2026-05-02) shipped an **MCP server with three privacy modes, disabled by default**. https://allume.com/memos/2026-07-allume-v4/
- **Braid** — `braid-http@1.4.11` (2026-08-10) and spec commits on a `versions-05` draft (2026-03), but the **IETF draft expired 2024-05-22 with no refresh**; `braidjs` last commit 2025-08-17. https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-toomim-httpbis-braid-http/history/
- **Willow / Earthstar — cold.** Latest spec news is 2025-10-26 (breaking changes to Confidential Sync and Drop Format); `willow-js` last commit 2025-03-26, `earthstar` 2024-08-08, JSR `@earthstar/meadowcap` last published 2024-05. **Meadowcap is still the best published capability-for-sync design — treat the spec as the asset, not the code.** https://willowprotocol.org/more/changes/index.html
- **Triplit — dormant.** Last release and last commit 2025; nothing in the window. https://github.com/aspen-cloud/triplit/commits/main
- **Veilid `v0.5.7` (2026-07-19)**, five releases in-window, commits through 2026-08-31 — but **every GitLab release description is just the version string. What changed: no source found.** https://gitlab.com/veilid/veilid/-/releases
- **Keet/Holepunch** — no app release feed found (**no source found** for Keet versions); modules move: `hyperdht` 6.33.2 + commits 2026-09-01, `hypercore` 11.35.2 (2026-08-20), `autobase` quiet since 2026-05-14. https://github.com/holepunchto/hyperdht/commits/main

