# 3. Capability / identity primitives

- **UCAN "1.0" is softer than it looks.** `ucan-wg/spec`, `delegation`, and `invocation` all committed *"Bump to v1.0.0 (drop RC.X)"* on **2026-07-08** — but the **latest git tag is still `v1.0-rc.1` and the repo has zero GitHub releases**. It is a README assertion, not a cut release. https://github.com/ucan-wg/spec/commits/main
- **UCAN revocation was left behind at rc.1** — last content commit 2025-07-14, no 1.0 bump. The one sub-spec a mesh most needs is the one that didn't ship. https://github.com/ucan-wg/revocation/commits/main
- **UCAN implementations are stalled**: `rs-ucan` has in-window commits (no_std, spec-deviation fixes, 2026-03-29) but **no release since 2023-06**; `go-ucan` v1.1.0 is 2025-10-29; `ucanto` `core-v10.4.6` is 2025-10-27; `ts-ucan` dead since 2023. https://github.com/ucan-wg/rs-ucan/releases
- **Biscuit** moved to the Eclipse Foundation (`biscuit-auth/*` → `eclipse-biscuit/*`). **Active commits, zero releases in the window** — latest crate is 6.0.0 (2025-07-16); spec repo last touched 2025-10-21. https://github.com/eclipse-biscuit/biscuit-rust/commits/main
- **ZCAP-LD unexpectedly reactivated** — 40 commits since 2026-03-01, clustered from 2026-07-16 and landing 2026-09-01. But it is all publishing plumbing (context-URL restructuring, semver aliases); still **v0.3.0 / v0.4.0-draft, no tags, no releases**, a CCG draft. https://github.com/w3c-ccg/zcap-spec/commits/main
- **KERI's code is healthy, its IETF specs are frozen.** keripy commits 2026-09-01, PyPI `keri` 1.3.6 (2026-07-31), keria 0.4.0 with ESSR hardening ("reject malformed ESSR payloads with 401", "make the ESSR tunnel byte-transparent"), signify-ts 0.4.0. But `draft-ssmith-keri` is still **rev 00 from 2024-01-28** and `draft-ssmith-cesr` rev 03 from 2024-02-01, both expired individual drafts. https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ssmith-keri/
- **DID Core 1.1 reached Candidate Recommendation Snapshot 2026-03-05**; **DID Resolution v1 reached CR Draft 2026-08-28** with exit criteria of two independent implementations per feature. **No new DID Recommendation was published in the window.** https://www.w3.org/TR/did-1.1/ · https://www.w3.org/TR/did-resolution/
- **`did:webvh`** was named by DIF + ToIP (June 2026) as one of the first two "recommended DID methods"; active through 2026-08-11 as a DIF Editors Draft, not W3C track. `did:key` has no movement since 2025-11-02. **`did:web` in-window: no source found.** https://blog.identity.foundation/two-recommended-did-methods/
- **OpenMLS 0.9.0 (2026-08-25)** — adds **PQ ciphersuites (P-384, ML-DSA)**, targeted messages, experimental virtual clients, safe-AAD; drops non-self-describing storage formats. **Two security fixes**: a bare `GroupContextExtensions` proposal could **bypass the `AppDataUpdate` immutability check** on `app_data_dictionary` (#2125), and wrong tree-node-index computation on invalid input (#2186). https://github.com/openmls/openmls/releases/tag/openmls-v0.9.0
- **mls-rs 0.56.0 (2026-08-19)** — crates.io is the only signal; the repo publishes no GitHub releases. https://crates.io/crates/mls-rs
- **No new MLS RFC in the window.** Six WG drafts revised though: `mls-partial` rev 02, `mls-pq-ciphersuites` rev 06, `mls-extensions` rev 10, and three newly WG-adopted (`virtual-clients`, `targeted-messages`, `ratchet-tree-options`). https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/mls/documents/
- **Decentralized MLS is the closest external analogue to BeeKEM.** `draft-kohbrok-mls-dmls` **rev 03, 2026-04-23** — retains key material to process Commits out-of-order with no central Delivery Service, built on the **FREEK fork-resilient CGKA** construction. `draft-xue-mls-decentralized` rev 00 (2026-07-01), presented at IETF 126. **Both still individual drafts, not WG-adopted.** https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-kohbrok-mls-dmls/
- **eprint 2026/1677, "Fair-Weather No More: Guaranteed Efficiency in Secure Group Messaging"** (Bartusek, Bitansky, Dodis, Garg, Wu), received 2026-08-13, major revision of a CRYPTO 2026 paper — CGKA efficiency under adversarial scheduling. https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/1677

*Correction to one sub-finding: Keyhive **does** publish tagged releases — `keyhive-wasm/0.1.0-alpha.8` (2026-08-18) and back through alpha.4. https://github.com/inkandswitch/keyhive/releases*

